// onsa.toml
// [test]
// spec = ["§4.5", "§15.1"]
// fixes = 0

// S-862 (W5-02 U5a, §15.1: "暗黙の prelude は … 種の制約 `Copy` と `Dup`（§4.6）、型パラメータの暗黙の要求 `Escape`（§4.5）…だけである。
// prelude の名前は隠せないので（§5.1）、同じ名前の項目（型、trait、関数、定数、flow）を宣言するか `use` で取り込むと E0304 になる"): `Escape`, the
// implicit requirement of a type parameter that a `?Escape` takes off (§4.5), is a name of the prelude like `Copy` and `Dup` (the case
// overlap_prelude_traits_effects), so an item of that name is E0304: a struct (`structure.onsa`), an enum (`enumeration.onsa`) and
// a type alias (`alias.onsa`). The `use` lines here take the item `Escape` of each of these modules, which is another E0304 in this
// file (the item is the E0304 in its own file). A function, a constant or a flow named `Escape` is not written: the name is also
// an E0320 (the names of those items are snake_case or UPPER_SNAKE, §2.3), which the syntax stage reports and the cases cannot
// pair with the E0304. The error has no candidate (`fixes = 0`). The bound `?Escape` is the E0200 of types/bounds_maybe_escape.onsa.
use structure.{Escape} //~ E0304
use enumeration.{Escape} //~ E0304
use alias.{Escape} //~ E0304

pub fn fine() -> I32 {
  1
}
